11	 * Makes the computed {@link MemberId member id} unique before the owner is saved. The id is a pure
12	 * function of region, fiscal year, telephone and last name, so two distinct owners can in principle
13	 * derive the same value; when the id collides with an existing owner's member id, the smallest
14	 * {@code n} of 2 or more is appended as {@code '-<n>'} (see {@link MemberId#dedupe(String, Set)}).
15	 * Runs after the id has been stamped by {@link BuildOwner} and before {@link SaveOwner}, mutating
16	 * the owner in place.
17	 */
18	public class DeduplicateMemberId {
